videos.script:
A program on your laptop runs until you close it. An app on a phone does not get that promise. {{pocket}}

The system decides when it runs, when it stops, and how much battery it may spend. The screen changes size when the phone turns. The network comes and goes in a lift. {{constraints}} This course is about those rules, and they are the same on both platforms.

Today you meet the two platforms, Android and iOS, and what really differs between them. {{two}} Then you set up the one thing this course needs on your computer: Node.js, to run the study planner's logic. {{node}} No phone, no Mac and no Android SDK. {{boundary}} The courses after the fork need those, and this lesson says which ones, now.
